What are Smart Contact Lenses?
Smart contact lenses represent a revolutionary advancement in the wearable technology and medical device sectors. These lenses incorporate sophisticated micro-electronics such as sensors and microchips to monitor physiological conditions like glucose levels or intraocular pressure, or to deliver therapeutic agents directly to the eye. As a sophisticated interface between the digital and biological worlds, they are designed to provide continuous, real-time health data while maintaining the primary function of vision correction. The core innovation lies in their ability to function as non-invasive diagnostic tools that transmit data wirelessly to healthcare providers. This technology creates a paradigm shift from reactive healthcare to proactive, preventative medicine by allowing for constant biomarker tracking.
